                <pb facs="0819" n="705" sameAs="frus:frus1924v01/pg705"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">822.61334/148: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Ecuador</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Bading</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Quito</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1924-12-02T11:00:00-05:14"><hi rendition="#italic">December 2,
                                1924—11 a.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received December 3—9:10
                        a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>19. Department’s telegram November 26, 6 p.m. From sources believed to be
                    reliable it is learned that all debts to local banks and <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >vale</hi> holders have been paid except one <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >vale</hi> in litigation.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Bading</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
